<h1>Limits</h1>
<p class="lead">The edge build is the Soli interpreter and the request pipeline, without the
server around them. What needs a socket, a thread, a subprocess or a disk stays with
<code>soli serve</code>.</p>

<div class="grid two">
  <article>
    <h2>Runs on the edge</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Routes, controllers, <code>before_action</code>, middleware</li>
      <li>Views, layouts, partials, components, view helpers</li>
      <li>Query strings, URL-encoded forms, JSON bodies and responses</li>
      <li>I18n from <code>config/locales</code></li>
      <li>Models on Cloudflare D1 or on SoliDB over HTTPS: <code>find</code>, <code>where</code>, <code>create</code>, <code>update</code>…</li>
      <li>The <code>HTTP</code> class, over the Worker's <code>fetch</code></li>
      <li>Static files from <code>public/</code>, served by Cloudflare</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h2>Stays with soli serve</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>WebSockets, LiveView, server-sent events and streamed bodies (answered with a 501)</li>
      <li>Background jobs, cron, mailers that send</li>
      <li>Multipart uploads and anything that writes files</li>
      <li>PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQLite and the native SoliDB driver; transactions on D1</li>
      <li><code>--dev</code>: hot reload, the dev bar, the REPL</li>
      <li>PDF, Office documents, lossy WebP encoding, subprocesses</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</div>

<h2>Worth knowing</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>One request at a time per isolate.</strong> A request suspended on a query keeps
      its isolate; Cloudflare spreads load over more isolates.</li>
  <li><strong>A Rust panic ends the isolate</strong>, where <code>soli serve</code> would answer
      a 500 and carry on. The next request boots a fresh one.</li>
  <li><strong>Size.</strong> About 3 MB compressed: inside the paid plan's limit, at the edge of
      the free one.</li>
  <li><strong>Sessions.</strong> The in-memory store lives as long as an isolate; use the
      <code>cookie</code> driver with <code>SOLI_SESSION_SECRET</code>.</li>
</ul>
